    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s September 1st slate, our offensive ceiling is anchored by **Bryce Harper** (72.33) and **Cal Raleigh** (72.28). **Bryce Harper** draws a favorable L/L matchup against Rodriguez, and his underlying xwOBA of .394 suggests he is poised to capitalize on the park factors. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** is our primary source of power potential today, facing an extremely vulnerable Paez (9.12 xERA). **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) also emerges as a high-value play; his score is significantly boosted by a +14% park factor and a +17% edge against the opposing starter, making him a critical component of today\u2019s strategy to secure power numbers.\n\nStrategic attention must be paid to our speed-focused assets. While **Zack Gelof** (56.17) carries a respectable score, his inclusion is prioritized for his +2% efficiency bump against a starter with a slow delivery, directly attacking our scarcity need in stolen bases. Conversely, **Jung Hoo Lee** (43.51) remains in the lineup despite a challenging matchup against Skenes (3.18 xERA). While Skenes is an elite arm, **Jung Hoo Lee** maintains a positive platoon adjustment that kept him above our \"Below floor\" threshold, though he is the most volatile asset in today's start. **Lawrence Butler** (48.15) sits on the lower end of our starting confidence interval; he was the final cut-line candidate, narrowly edging out depth pieces on the bench due to his favorable #3 spot in the order, though his heavy negative platoon shift against Gore suggests he is a candidate for a late-game sub if the game script turns early.\n\nRisks remain present across the board, particularly for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (53.95), whose score is suppressed by a -19% SP skill penalty against Miles. We are navigating these matchups while waiting for better health news on **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman**, both of whom remain shelved. With **Justin Crawford** and **Tyler Freeman** currently unavailable, we have limited flexibility to pivot if these projections falter. We are banking on **Luis Arraez** (58.51) to provide stability; his +14% SP skill advantage against Rodriguez serves as the primary hedge against the volatility inherent in starting **Yainer Diaz** (46.02) and **Gleyber Torres** (45.32), both of whom are essentially fighting to maintain positive value today.",
